  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flood Risk Mitigation and Management Technical Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate-induced floods have heavily impacted South Sudan from 2019 to 2021. In each of these years, close to 1 million people lost businesses, farms, animals, belongings and homes and had to seek safety in other places (away from their homes). Most affected areas are within the Sudd Valley, along the White Nile. They include, among others, Bentiu, Bor, Ayod, Fangak, Bor, Pibor and Malakal. These floods have severely affected the ability of South Sudan to recover from the effects of years of civil conflict and build resilience. It has been exacerbating the already dire humanitarian situation in the country. Unfortunately, the flooding pattern repeated in 2022, with over a million people affected countrywide. This project aims to provide technical advice on surface water and flood management to local government institutions, the South Sudan Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs and Disaster Management (MHADM), the International Organization for Migration (IOM), United Nations Mission in South Sudan (UNMISS) and the United Nations World Food Programme (WFP) in the targeted areas responding to floods in South Sudan. This technical support is expected to lead to concrete interventions carried out by the private sector in Bentiu.</narrative>
  </description>
